+# Mirror Sync Stability / Repo Cleanup Implementation Plan
+
+> For Codex: implement this plan in the target checkout and keep the diff localized/reviewable. Do not commit.
+
+**Goal:** Stop noisy/repeated mirror sync failures and misleading mainnode/channel spam by validating/deduplicating repository records, fixing repo-name derivation, hardening mirror-path handling, and reducing unnecessary encrypted channel frames.
+
+**Target checkout:** `/Users/mdkaifansari04/code/forkmesh-root/forkmesh-v0.5.0`
+
+**Primary files likely to touch:**
+- `qt_client/src/MainWindow.cpp`
+- `qt_client/src/MainWindow.h` only if a helper/member declaration is necessary
+- `qt_client/src/ServerNode.cpp`
+- `qt_client/src/ServerNode.h` only if reconnect-stability state is added
+- Optional test/docs only if very small and clearly useful
+
+**Required verification:**
+- `cd qt_client && ./run.sh test`
+- `git diff --check -- qt_client/src/MainWindow.cpp qt_client/src/MainWindow.h qt_client/src/ServerNode.cpp qt_client/src/ServerNode.h agents/mirror-sync-stability.md`
+
+---
+
+## 0. Context and root-cause analysis
+
+The user pasted Qt network/mirror logs showing several symptoms:
+
+1. Repeated channel messages on connect:
+   - `Network: sent encrypted channel through mainnode room general.` repeated many times.
+   - Current code in `MainWindow::startSession()` calls `m_backend->addChannel(repositoryChannel(repo))` for every repository immediately after `ServerNode::start()`.
+   - `ServerNode::addChannel()` always sends a `channel` frame, even when the channel already exists and even when the WebSocket is not ready. `sendEncrypted()` logs activity even when `sendTextFrame()` drops the frame because `m_wsReady == false`.
+   - Root cause: channel frames are sent/logged for duplicates and before connection readiness. The eventual `hello` already advertises channel membership.
+
+2. Repeated host-serving lines:
+   - `Host: serving mdkaifansari/repository live to the web.` repeated several times.
+   - `startRepoHosts()` correctly calls `stopRepoHosts()`, so this is mostly caused by duplicate/stale repository records with the same effective published owner/name and sometimes same mirror path.
+
+3. Repeated sync failures for a local path:
+   - `fatal: '/Users/mdkaifansari04/code/forkmesh-updated/' does not appear to be a git repository`
+   - Current `syncRepository()` blindly tries to `git clone --mirror` or `git fetch --prune` using `repositorySource(repo)` without revalidating local source existence/Git-ness. Auto-sync retries every broken record.
+   - Evidence from the live QSettings on this machine showed stale rows pointing to `/Users/mdkaifansari04/code/forkmesh-updated/`, which does not exist in this checkout layout.
+
+4. Destination path collisions:
+   - `fatal: destination path '.../mirrors/newnewnode-forkmesh.git' already exists and is not an empty directory`
+   - Evidence from QSettings showed duplicated/colliding records such as two `forkmesh` entries sharing the same `newnewnode-forkmesh.git` mirror path, plus several `mdkaifansari/repository` records sharing mirror paths.
+   - Current loading/saving allows duplicates by owner/name, by effective published owner/name, and by mirror path. `promptAddRepository()` also does not check for duplicate `owner/name` before appending.
+
+5. Bad default repo name from local folders ending in `/`:
+   - `repoNameFromUrl()` currently uses `url.section('/', -1)`. For paths ending in `/`, that returns empty and falls back to `repository`.
+   - This is why unrelated local folders can all become `repository`, causing catalog/host/mirror collisions.
+
+6. Fast reconnect loops after short-lived connections:
+   - Logs show repeated `TLS/SSL connection has been closed`, immediate reconnects, and status reset loops.
+   - `ServerNode` resets `m_reconnectAttempt = 0` as soon as it sees HTTP 101. If the socket closes seconds later, the next retry is back at the minimum delay. This can hammer the mainnode during unstable periods.
+
+Do not change protocol/signature behavior, Worker routes, or the Worker itself for this task.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Fix repo-name derivation from paths/URLs
+
+Problem:
+- `repoNameFromUrl("/Users/me/project/")` becomes `repository`.
+
+Implementation guidance:
+- Update `repoNameFromUrl(QString url)` in `MainWindow.cpp` so it:
+  1. trims whitespace;
+  2. replaces `\\` with `/`;
+  3. strips trailing `/` characters except for root `/`;
+  4. then takes the final segment;
+  5. strips `.git`;
+  6. passes through `repoSegment(name, "repository")`.
+- This should make `/Users/me/Chat-App/` become `chat-app`, `/Users/me/dsa/` become `dsa`, and `https://forkmesh.com/newnewnode/forkmesh` become `forkmesh`.
+
+Keep behavior simple; no new dependencies.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Add small repository/mirror validation helpers
+
+Add local helpers in `MainWindow.cpp` anonymous namespace where practical. Suggested helpers:
+
+- `bool pathIsGitRepository(const QString &path)`:
+  - true for normal worktrees: `.git` exists under the directory;
+  - true for bare mirrors: `HEAD` and `objects` exist;
+  - false for missing/empty path.
+
+- `bool mirrorPathIsUsableBareRepo(const QString &path)`:
+  - use a short `git -C <path> rev-parse --is-bare-repository` process or filesystem checks (`HEAD`, `objects`) if you want to avoid process overhead;
+  - only true for an existing bare mirror.
+
+- `QString mirrorPathFor(const QString &root, const QString &owner, const QString &name)` or inline equivalent:
+  - `root + "/" + repoSegment(owner, "owner") + "-" + repoSegment(name, "repository") + ".git"`.
+
+- `QString repoKey(const RepositoryRecord &repo)`:
+  - `repoSegment(repo.owner, "owner") + "/" + repoSegment(repo.name, "repository")`.
+
+- `QString publishedKeyFor(const RepositoryRecord &repo)` may be useful:
+  - if using catalog-owner semantics, effective publish key is `catalogOwner(repo) + "/" + repoSegment(repo.name, "repository")`.
+  - Be careful: `catalogOwner()` is a member function, so this one may belong inside member code instead of anonymous namespace.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Normalize and dedupe repository records on load
+
+Current `loadRepositories()` appends every persisted row if `name` and `repositorySource(repo)` are non-empty. That:
+- drops valid mirror-only forks after restart if they have a mirror but no source;
+- keeps duplicate/stale rows forever;
+- keeps invalid local paths forever;
+- allows several rows to share one mirror path.
+
+Update `loadRepositories()` to normalize and self-heal in memory, then persist if anything changed.
+
+Desired behavior:
+
+1. Normalize owner/name fields:
+   - `repo.owner = repoSegment(repo.owner, "owner")`
+   - `repo.name = repoSegment(repo.name, repoNameFromUrl(repositorySource(repo)))` or at least `repoSegment(repo.name, "repository")`.
+   - If `repo.name == "repository"` and `repo.localPath` has a real final directory name, consider replacing with `repoNameFromUrl(repo.localPath)` to repair old trailing-slash fallback records.
+   - Be conservative: do not rename a non-`repository` name.
+
+2. Keep records if they are useful:
+   - source is non-empty and valid enough to try later, OR
+   - mirrorPath points to an existing usable bare repo.
+   - Do not keep records with empty name and no source/mirror.
+
+3. Validate local source paths:
+   - If `repo.localPath` is non-empty but missing/not Git, keep the record only if it has a usable existing mirror; otherwise skip it as stale.
+   - If kept only because mirror exists, future auto-sync should not repeatedly fetch the invalid source.
+
+4. Dedupe duplicate records:
+   - Dedupe exact repo keys (`owner/name`) by merging into the best record.
+   - Also avoid multiple published records with the same effective published key (`catalogOwner/name`) because they will all try to host/publish the same public repo.
+   - Prefer the record with a usable mirror and most recent `lastSyncMs`/`publishedAtMs`.
+   - Preserve useful fields when merging: description, bchAddress, cloneUrl/localPath if valid, publishToNetwork OR, actionsEnabled if either enabled, max timestamps.
+
+5. Mirror path collisions:
+   - If two records share `mirrorPath`, only one should keep that path unless they are the same merged repo.
+   - For a record with a missing/nonexistent colliding path, rewrite to the expected unique mirror path for its owner/name.
+   - If the expected mirror path already exists and is a valid mirror for another record, create a deterministic suffix (`owner-name-2.git`, etc.) or skip with a log. Prefer minimal deterministic behavior.
+
+6. Persist once if normalization/dedupe changed anything:
+   - call `saveRepositories()` after `settings.endArray()` if changed.
+   - log a concise line such as `Repository settings: cleaned up N duplicate/stale mirror entries.`
+
+Do not delete any filesystem directories in this task.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Prevent duplicate appends when adding/mirroring/forking repos
+
+Update append paths:
+- `promptAddRepository()`
+- `mirrorCatalogRepo()`
+- `mirrorAdvertisedRepo()`
+- `forkCurrentRepo()`
+
+Behavior:
+- Before appending, check existing records for same effective key and/or same normalized localPath/cloneUrl.
+- If duplicate exists, do not append another row. Instead log/flash `Already mirroring owner/name` and optionally select/open the existing repo.
+- When choosing a mirror path, avoid collisions using the helper from section 3.
+- For local repos, after `QFileDialog::getExistingDirectory`, normalize/clean the path before name extraction so trailing slash does not create `repository`.
+
+Keep UI simple; no new dialogs beyond existing warnings.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Harden syncRepository / autoSyncMirrors
+
+Current `autoSyncMirrors()` retries broken local paths and clone URL failures forever.
+
+Minimal robust behavior:
+
+1. In `syncRepository(int index, bool quiet)`:
+   - Compute source once.
+   - If `repo.localPath` is non-empty and not a Git repo:
+     - for manual sync (`quiet == false`), flash/log an actionable message: `Local source for owner/name is missing or not a Git repository: <path>`;
+     - for auto-sync (`quiet == true`), skip without spamming every timer tick. A small one-time log per app session is okay if you add a set of already-reported broken repos; otherwise keep it silent for quiet mode.
+     - return before running git.
+   - If source is empty and mirror exists, skip fetch unless the mirror has an origin remote; mirror-only forks should not auto-sync upstream.
+
+2. Distinguish bare mirror validity from directory existence:
+   - `hasMirror` should mean usable bare repo, not just `QDir(repo.mirrorPath).exists()`.
+   - If the target mirror path exists but is not a usable bare repo and is non-empty:
+     - do not run `git clone` into it;
+     - report `Mirror path exists but is not a bare Git mirror: <path>`;
+     - choose a new unique path only if safe and clear, or require user action. Prefer no destructive cleanup.
+
+3. In `autoSyncMirrors()`:
+   - skip invalid local sources and mirror-only forks with no clone URL/origin;
+   - do not auto-sync records already in `m_syncingRepos`.
+
+4. Keep successful sync behavior unchanged:
+   - save `lastSyncMs`;
+   - install hook;
+   - publish and start hosts if changed/published.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Reduce mainnode channel/log spam in ServerNode
+
+Change `ServerNode::addChannel()`:
+
+Current bug:
+```cpp
+if (!m_channels.contains(name)) {
+    m_channels.append(name);
+    emit channelsChanged(m_channels);
+}
+QJsonObject message = makeMessage("channel");
+...
+sendEncrypted(message, true);
+```
+
+New behavior:
+- If normalized channel is empty, return.
+- If channel already exists, return without sending/logging.
+- If channel is new, append and emit `channelsChanged`.
+- Only send the `channel` frame when `m_wsReady` is true. If the socket is not ready, the next `sendHello()` will advertise all channels, so nothing is lost.
+
+This removes the misleading startup `Network: sent encrypted channel...` burst.
+
+Optional: consider making `setMirroredRepos()` use a deduped/sorted list before comparing/sending hello. This prevents repeated `hello` frames if only order/duplicates changed.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Tame reconnect backoff for short-lived connections
+
+Current behavior resets `m_reconnectAttempt = 0` as soon as a 101 upgrade succeeds. In the logs, connections can close quickly afterward, causing repeated minimum-delay reconnects.
+
+Implement a small stability threshold:
+- Add `qint64 m_connectedSinceMs = 0;` to `ServerNode`.
+- On successful WebSocket upgrade, set `m_connectedSinceMs = currentMSecsSinceEpoch()` but do not immediately reset `m_reconnectAttempt`, OR reset only if the previous attempt was already stable.
+- On disconnect, compute connection duration:
+  - if duration is greater than e.g. 60 seconds, reset/reduce backoff;
+  - if duration is short, keep/increment backoff so repeated short closes back off progressively.
+- On user shutdown, preserve existing behavior (no reconnect).
+
+Keep this small. Do not change WebSocket protocol bytes, encryption, ping frame format, or message envelope.
+
+---
+
+## 8. Tests / verification expectations
+
+At minimum run:
+```sh
+cd qt_client
+./run.sh test
+```
+
+Also run:
+```sh
+git diff --check -- qt_client/src/MainWindow.cpp qt_client/src/MainWindow.h qt_client/src/ServerNode.cpp qt_client/src/ServerNode.h agents/mirror-sync-stability.md
+```
+
+If you can add a tiny test without broad refactoring, add one. Good candidates:
+- `repoNameFromUrl("/Users/me/Chat-App/") == "chat-app"`
+- duplicate load/merge helper if you factor it into a testable function.
+
+But do not over-refactor just to test private UI code. Build/test passing is acceptable if the fix remains localized.
+
+---
+
+## 9. Final report requirements
+
+Report:
+- exact files changed;
+- which log symptoms each change addresses;
+- what remains a user-data cleanup vs code fix;
+- verification commands and results.
+
+Do not commit.
+
+## Implementation Status
+
+Status: implemented by Codex, then manually unblocked after Codex hung during final response/test reporting.
+
+Files changed for this task:
+- `qt_client/CMakeLists.txt`
+- `qt_client/src/MainWindow.cpp`
+- `qt_client/src/MainWindow.h`
+- `qt_client/src/ServerNode.cpp`
+- `qt_client/src/ServerNode.h`
+- `qt_client/tests/test_window.cpp`
+- `agents/mirror-sync-stability.md`
+
+What landed:
+- Fixed trailing-slash repo name derivation so local folders like `Chat-App/` no longer become the fallback `repository`.
+- Added repository source/mirror validation helpers and used them in sync, hosting, insights, actions workflow discovery, stats, and hooks.
+- `loadRepositories()` now normalizes/dedupes stale QSettings repo records, drops invalid local-path-only rows, keeps valid mirror-only rows, merges duplicate repo records, and avoids mirror path collisions.
+- Add/mirror/fork paths now detect existing repo/source/effective published keys before appending another duplicate record.
+- `syncRepository()` now skips invalid local sources before running git and refuses non-empty non-bare mirror targets with an actionable error instead of producing raw git clone/fetch failures.
+- `autoSyncMirrors()` now skips invalid local paths and mirror-only forks without an origin, reducing repeated background failures.
+- `startRepoHosts()` now dedupes by effective published repo key so duplicate records do not spawn repeated host tunnels/log lines.
+- `ServerNode::addChannel()` only sends/logs channel frames for newly-added channels and only after the WebSocket is ready; startup channels are advertised by `hello`.
+- `ServerNode::setMirroredRepos()` dedupes/sorts before sending hello updates.
+- Reconnect backoff no longer resets immediately on HTTP 101; short-lived closes back off progressively, while stable connections reset after the stability threshold.
+- Added a regression in `qt_client/tests/test_window.cpp` for stale duplicate repository settings and trailing-slash name normalization.
+- Codex also moved the local mirror remote display into a GitHub-style `Code` menu button instead of the previous inline local-remote row; this compiles and is covered by the window smoke test.
+
+Verification:
+- `cd qt_client && ./run.sh test` — passed.
+- `git diff --check -- qt_client/CMakeLists.txt qt_client/src/MainWindow.cpp qt_client/src/MainWindow.h qt_client/src/ServerNode.cpp qt_client/src/ServerNode.h qt_client/tests/test_window.cpp agents/mirror-sync-stability.md` — passed.
+- Added-line static scan — no real issue; it only matched Qt `QMenu::exec(...)` as a false positive for the word `exec`.
+- Independent reviewer verdict — passed. Suggestions were non-blocking: add more coverage later for mirror collision, duplicate append paths, reconnect backoff, symlink/case-equivalent paths, conservative cleanup of unmounted local repos, and better skipped-sync visibility.
+
+Notes:
+- No Worker/protocol/signature behavior was changed for this task.
+- Existing user settings may still contain old duplicate/stale rows until the rebuilt app starts once; the new `loadRepositories()` path will normalize and persist cleanup in-app.
+- I did not delete any mirror directories or mutate macOS QSettings manually.
