+# Qt Repo Code Menu Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Reduce repo detail header clutter by moving the local remote URL into a GitHub-style Code dropdown.
+
+**Architecture:** Keep the existing repo detail header and tab stack. Add one `Code` action button to the header row, populate a `QMenu` on click with the local mirror path and copy action, remove the always-visible local remote row, and condense status/date metadata into a compact two-column band.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Qt 6 Widgets, existing `MainWindow` UI code, existing headless `forkmesh-window-tests`.
+
+---
+
+## File Structure
+
+- Modify: `../qt_client/tests/test_window.cpp` to assert the new header shape.
+- Modify: `../qt_client/src/MainWindow.h` to add the `Code` button member and small helper methods.
+- Modify: `../qt_client/src/MainWindow.cpp` to add the Code dropdown and compact status labels.
+- Modify: `../qt_client/src/Theme.h` only if the new compact status labels need object-name styling.
+
+## Task 1: Add The UI Smoke Test
+
+- [ ] Add a test in `../qt_client/tests/test_window.cpp` that finds `repoCodeButton`.
+- [ ] Add a test that no visible label text contains `LOCAL REMOTE`.
+- [ ] Run `../qt_client/run.sh test` and verify the window test fails because the Code button is missing and the old remote label still exists.
+
+## Task 2: Add The Code Dropdown
